2026-11-12T00:55:11.3076442Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3183315Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3193293Z [0m
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3193882Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3194920Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3195307Z 
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3195649Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3196492Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3196939Z 
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3197246Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3198582Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3198921Z 
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3199537Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3200455Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3201194Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3201800Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3202084Z 
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3202362Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3202818Z 
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3203151Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3203722Z    can use Nix.
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3203870Z 
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3203977Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3204455Z 
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3204804Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3205332Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3208121Z 
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3208316Z I will:
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3208540Z 
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3209030Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3209646Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3210050Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3210412Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3210668Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3210907Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3211283Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3211629Z    /root
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3225828Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3226559Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3237641Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3238173Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3238996Z 
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3240059Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3240628Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3260895Z 
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3261475Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3272779Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3273387Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3273945Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3274434Z 
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3274657Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3274926Z 
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3275288Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3275860Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3276096Z 
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3276201Z If you would like to
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3276499Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3276711Z 
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3276930Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3277462Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-12T00:55:11.3277673Z 
